UID:9489e6962af21c5140e2da97557e825c10302026_1:34:47_PM@campusgroups.com
SUMMARY;ENCODING=QUOTED-PRINTABLE:Día de Los Muertos | Day of the Dead Celebration
LOCATION:Latin American and Caribbean Studies Center- Social and Behavioral Sciences Building, Room N335, United States
URL:https://sbengaged.stonybrook.edu/rsvp?id=391627
DESCRIPTION:Día de los Muertos | Day of the Dead Celebration\nDate: Monday, November 2nd, 2026\nTime: 12:30-1:45 PM\nLocation: Latin American & Caribbean Studies Center- Social and Behavioral Sciences Building, Room N335\n\nJoin us as we honor and celebrate Día de Los Muertos (Day of the Dead) — a vibrant cultural tradition that pays tribute to the lives and memories of our loved ones who have passed. Although Día de los Muertos is celebrated throughout Latin America, it has deep pre-colonial indigenous roots.\n\nGuests are invited to contribute photos or small offerings to a community ofrenda (altar) in remembrance of family, friends, and historical/cultural icons who have inspired them. Honor and celebrate your departed loved ones (human and animal) over lunch, marigolds, Spanish poetry, and mingling at our altar! Tacos and pan provided\n\nEnjoy Latin American refreshments as we come together to celebrate life, legacy, and cultural tradition. \n\nThis event is free and open to all.\n\nSponsored by:\nHispanic Heritage Month Committee\nDiversity, Intercultural and Community Engagement (DICE)\nLatin American and Caribbean Studies Center (LACS)\nDepartment of Hispanic Languages and Literature (HLL)\nDress Code: Casual (jeans ok)\n---\nEvent Details: https://sbengaged.stonybrook.edu/rsvp?id=391627
END:VEVENT
